---
description: Core context and hard rules for llm-serving-bench
alwaysApply: true
---

Read @PROJECT_BRIEF.md before doing any work in this repo. It is the source
of truth for scope, hardware plan, measurement protocol, and phase gates.

Hard rules that override any instruction to the contrary:

1. Every number that leaves this project must be traceable to a logged run in
   results/benchmarks.csv. Never invent, estimate, or extrapolate a benchmark
   figure. If a run has not happened, say so.
2. Every row in benchmarks.csv must have a `hardware` value. Valid values:
   kaggle_t4_x1, kaggle_t4_x2, aws_<instance_type>. Never log a laptop timing
   as a result. Never present a T4 number as an AWS number.
3. This repo measures throughput, latency, and cost only. It does not measure
   accuracy. Do not import, restate, or reason about SourceBound's accuracy
   figures.
4. Do not expand scope. Out of scope: speculative decoding, multi-node serving,
   any UI, fine-tuning, accuracy evaluation, recommender systems. If a change
   would add one of these, stop and flag it instead of implementing it.
5. AWS budget ceiling is $25 total. Public subnet only, no NAT Gateway. Spot
   instances only. Never write Terraform that provisions on-demand GPU or a
   NAT Gateway. Always leave the stack destroyable in one `terraform destroy`.
6. Pick one model in Phase 0 and never change it. Changing models invalidates
   every prior measurement.
7. Do not start a phase until the previous phase's definition of done in
   PROJECT_BRIEF.md §11 is met. State which phase you are in before working.
8. Negative results are first-class output. When an optimization rung does not
   help, record it in the CSV notes column and write up why.
